      "sourceTextSha256": "4e58ef7b4e3cd6d9ae6fbc349ed4e499c07054e98f45d7c910414e760950dfe9",
      "text": "Day 2 · Breakfast at the hotel. Guided city tour (4 hours) with an English-speaking guide, through a capital of elegant architecture and centuries-old culture, known for its many museums, galleries and theatres. Discover the old neighbourhood of La Boca and historic San Telmo, with its bars, restaurants and the antiques market on Plaza Dorrego, then Plaza de Mayo, the heart of the city, with the Casa Rosada, the presidential palace associated with Eva Perón.\n\nSee the 67-metre Obelisk, symbol of the city, on Avenida 9 de Julio, one of the widest avenues in the world, and the elegant Recoleta district with its famous cemetery and the colonial-style church of El Pilar, before visiting modern Puerto Madero.",
